WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.340
Among all kinds of pain that a human goes
through, Child birth is generally

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.280
considered to be the most severe.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.280
Yes!

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.450
The pain that a female goes through is
unbearable.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.840
So we have all given our mother that intense
pain while coming

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.810
into this world.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.760
But have you ever wondered about how you got
this life?

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.320
What were the series
of steps that made you grow into this structure

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.009
from being a single cell?

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:35.780
Let’s have a look at this most important
process that helped us gain life.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.780
Yes!

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.960
I am referring to the process of FERTILIZATION!

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.710
How do we define it in simplest words?

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.900
Fertilization is the process in which a male
gamete fuses with a female gamete

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.990
giving rise to a zygote.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.100
So how will this process begin?

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.990
When one sperm among all the others is able
to penetrate the egg cell then the egg releases

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.310
certain chemicals.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:03.870
These
chemicals make sure that no other sperm will

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.250
now penetrate this egg.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.399
The first step begins now when the male nucleus
from the sperm fuses with

00:01:10.399 --> 00:01:16.009
the female nucleus that is already sitting
right there in the big fat egg cell.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:20.289
The fusion stimulates a cascade of reactions
which will further give rise to

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:23.299
several successive cell divisions.

00:01:23.299 --> 00:01:26.009
The consecutive cell divisions then give rise
to

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:30.289
an EMBRYO that will further develop into an
ORGANISM.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:35.509
So is this process of fertilization the same
in all the organisms?

00:01:35.509 --> 00:01:37.030
Think for a
moment!

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:40.719
In order to answer this question, we have
to keep in mind two major

00:01:40.719 --> 00:01:41.719
facts.

00:01:41.719 --> 00:01:46.450
Firstly, the process of fertilization is simply
the fusion of gametes.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.639
Secondly, the place where the fusion of gametes
can take place may be

00:01:50.639 --> 00:01:53.299
different in various organisms.

00:01:53.299 --> 00:01:55.810
So now can we answer the question correctly?

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:56.810
Yes!

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:02.719
The simplest answer is that the PROCESS of
fertilization will almost be the

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:03.719
same.

00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:07.219
This is because it involves the FUSION OF
GAMETES.

00:02:07.219 --> 00:02:12.600
However the LOCATION where fertilization occurs
may be different in animals.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.530
For example in humans the baby grows inside
the mother’s body.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.120
However,
have you seen babies of frogs?

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.030
They are not born from inside the body of
female frogs like in our case.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.730
This gets us to the concept of types of fertilization.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:33.550
The first example explains that fertilization
occurs INSIDE the FEMALE’S BODY.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:38.100
Hence such a type is referred to as INTERNAL
FERTILIZATION.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.920
In this case the
sperms from a male’s body enter the female’s

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.330
reproductive tract and reach the
fallopian tubes where the egg cell awaits.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:52.340
The fusion of both completes the
fertilization process inside her body.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.070
All higher animals like mammals exhibit
this type of fertilization.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.000
Now can you guess the next type?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Yes!

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.010
It will be EXTERNAL FERTILIZATION.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.860
As
the name says, the process will involve fusion

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:09.940
of gametes OUTSIDE the
FEMALE’S BODY.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.990
Frogs are examples belonging to this category.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:16.760
In this case,
the unfertilized eggs are released in the

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.070
water.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:21.980
Now the sperms from the male
body will be released on these eggs and will

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.010
fertilize them.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.890
As a result the
fertilization process will be accomplished

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.120
in the water outside the female’s
body!

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:35.880
Many aquatic animals including fishes exhibit
this type of fertilization.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.730
This is how fertilization takes place in animals.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:44.850
Now the most important thing
we need to know is how the embryo develops!

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.840
Do watch our next video to know this important
process.

